id: API-020
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 3
action: advisory
title: CRUD verbs in REST URL paths
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .py .java .go .rb
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
  content_contains: api
patterns:
  - regex: \.(get|post|put|delete|patch)\(['"`]\/[^'"]*\/(create|delete|update|remove|add|edit|modify|fetch|get)[A-Z]
    message: "CRUD verb in URL path — use nouns and HTTP methods instead (/users, not /createUser)"
fix: Use resource nouns with HTTP methods. POST /users (create), GET /users/:id (read), PUT /users/:id (update), DELETE /users/:id (delete).
